# Delete repo session

`C-d` should be available for a repo-backed named workspace entry even when
there is no live tmux session to close. Confirming should forget the workspace
and delete the workspace checkout.

Create `beta` and its named `feature` workspace with distinct descriptions, but
no attached tmux sessions. The repository glob supplies both picker entries.

    :b jj tmux cat sh sleep (available)
    :cp tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ -q jj git init beta (exit: 0)
    :$ -q jj describe -R beta -m "beta commit" (exit: 0)
    :$ -q jj workspace add -R beta --name feature beta.feature (exit: 0)
    :$ -q jj describe -R beta.feature -m "feature commit" (exit: 0)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth -r 'beta*'; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 12 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

Filter to the repo-only named workspace entry. The footer should offer deletion
even though the selected row has no live tmux sigil.

    :k feature
    :snap -d 2s -e '1/4' -e beta/feature -e 'C-d. delete' "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: feature
  1/4 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  beta/feature                             ~/beta.feature                                                             ┃
 [C-d] delete
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt feature@ hhhhhhhh
│  (empty) feature commit
│ ○  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt default@ hhhhhhhh
├─╯  (empty) beta commit
◆  wwwwwwww root() hhhhhhhh


```

Pressing `C-d` should mark the repo entry for deletion.

    :k C-d
    :snap -d 2s -e '1 session' --color "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: feature
  1/4 | [C-r] repo: none
▌× beta/feature                             ~/beta.feature                                                             ┃
 [C-d] unstage                                                                       delete [C-y] 1 session [C-g] cancel
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt feature@ hhhhhhhh
│  (empty) feature commit
│ ○  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt default@ hhhhhhhh
├─╯  (empty) beta commit
◆  wwwwwwww root() hhhhhhhh


```

![light](delete-repo-session.md.snap.2.light.svg)
![dark](delete-repo-session.md.snap.2.dark.svg)

Confirming should leave the picker alive, forget the workspace, and remove the
workspace checkout.

    :k C-y
    :$ sh -c 'i=0; while test -d beta.feature; do i=$((i+1)); test "$$i" -lt 100 || exit 1; sleep 0.05; done' (exit: 0)
    :snap -d 2s -e '0/3' "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: feature
  0/3 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  feature                                                                                                        tmux ┃

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────







```

    :$ sh -c 'test ! -e beta.feature' (exit: 0)
    :$ jj workspace list -R beta --ignore-working-copy --no-pager --color never --template 'name ++ "\n"' (exit: 0)

